note community/30page.om -- the pages: /community/ (what joining does, the one line, the rule, every
note published part with its record), /community/part/<id> (the developer view: every counted key
note with its time and fingerprints), and the record line the salvage part page shows.

text cmbase "<div class=\"sl\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">INTERPLANE / COMMUNITY MACHINES</p>"
text cmclose "</div>"
text cmh1 "<h1>"
text cmh1e "</h1>"
text cmh2 "<h2>"
text cmh2e "</h2>"
text cmp "<p>"
text cmpe "</p>"
text cmpre "<pre>"
text cmtdist "dist/"
text cmtsums "SHA256SUMS"
text cmcmh "Community machines"
text cmolder "Earlier parts of the ledger, the refusal log and the alarm log (each set aside at 4 MiB):"
text cmpree "</pre>"
text cmcode "<code>"
text cmcodee "</code>"
text cmhref "<a href=\""
text cmhrefe "\">"
text cmae "</a>"
text cmcard "<article class=\"sl-card\">"
text cmcarde "</article>"
text cmslug "community/"
text cmslpart "community/part/"
text cmslkey "community/key/"
text cmslmsg "community/msg/"
text cmslsal "salvage/"
text cmtitle "Run Interplane's checks on your own computer"
text cmintro "Anyone with an NVIDIA DGX Spark, or another 64-bit ARM computer running Linux, can lend it to Interplane. It asks for small public programs, builds each one and runs its example in a sealed box, and reports what it got. When several runners get the same bytes, everyone can see it here."
text cmjoinh "Join with one line"
text cmjoin "curl -fsSL https://interplane.io/community/join | sh"
text cmjoinp "It puts two files in a folder called .interplane-runner in your home folder, shows their SHA-256 fingerprints (compare them with the list at the bottom of this page), explains what will happen, and asks you to type yes before anything is registered. Nothing else needs to be installed."
text cmdoesh "What it does to your computer"
text cmdoes "<ul><li>It only makes outgoing requests to interplane.io. Nothing from outside can connect to your computer.</li><li>Each check takes at most 2 seconds of one CPU core to build and 2 to run, 128 MiB of address space (the most memory it can reserve), 1 MiB of output, and 3 seconds of clock time for each step.</li><li>You choose how many checks an hour: 30 to start, change it any time with <code>interplane-runner set rate N</code>, and 0 pauses.</li><li>Everything it keeps is in one folder, under 10 MiB. The secret half of its key never leaves your computer.</li><li>It does not start again by itself after a restart: run <code>interplane-runner start</code>.</li></ul>"
text cmneverh "What it can never do"
text cmnever "A checked program runs in a sealed box made by the Linux kernel: no network, none of your files, no environment variables, no GPU, no new processes. It can only read its example input and write its output. The runner runs nothing else from Interplane."
text cmstoph "Stop or leave"
text cmstop "~/.interplane-runner/bin/interplane-runner stop\n~/.interplane-runner/bin/interplane-runner leave"
text cmstopp "stop pauses it. leave stops it, tells Interplane, and deletes the folder."
text cmruleh "How results are counted"
text cmrule "Each runner is a key. One computer can hold several runners, and Interplane cannot tell from outside, so runners are counted, not machines. A key counts once for each revision of a part, however often it sends a result. Results agree when the built program, its output and its exit status are the same, byte for byte. Keys are free to make, so any number of agreeing keys is not called verified: agreement shows that the same bytes came back from every agreeing key, and if at least one of those keys is honest and used the pinned compiler, that runner really got them. It never changes what Interplane's own check says. Any disagreement is shown, and then the part is not presented as reproduced."
text cmpartsh "Published parts and their reruns"
text cmnopart "No part is published in the salvage yard yet."
text cmdevh "For developers"
text cmdev "The protocol, the runner's source and its gates are in spark-connector, <code>rad:z2LKDxnAK3EFfqgr7HTZh6djts65P</code>. Every accepted message and every refusal is kept:"
text cmled "community/ledger\">ledger</a> &#183; <a href=\""
text cmrefl "community/refused\">refusals</a> &#183; <a href=\""
text cmsums "community/dl/SHA256SUMS\">SHA256SUMS</a></p>"
text cmfilesh "Files and fingerprints"
text cmr0 "Not run again by community runners yet."
text cmr1 "Ran again by "
text cmr2 " community runner"
text cmr2s " community runners"
text cmr3 ": "
text cmr4 " agree"
text cmr5 ", "
text cmr6 " disagree. While results disagree this part is not presented as reproduced."
text cmr7 " No single result has more runners than every other."
text cmplath "Which computers can join"
text cmplat "<ul><li>Linux on 64-bit ARM (aarch64), such as an NVIDIA DGX Spark: works. Interplane runs it on its own DGX Spark.</li><li>Linux on x86-64, most PCs and servers: not covered yet. The compiler cannot yet build the sealed box for x86-64; the gap is with the compiler's owner.</li><li>Mac: not covered. The sealed box is made with Linux kernel features (Landlock and seccomp) that macOS does not have.</li></ul><p>On a computer that is not covered, the join line says so and installs nothing.</p>"
text cmrunh "Runners now"
text cmrun1 " runner"
text cmrun1s " runners"
text cmrun2 " registered: keys that joined and have not left (a key Interplane has refused since still counts here). Several runners can be on one computer."
text cmnoteh "Interplane's note on its own runners: "
text cmtnote "runners-note"
text cmrtab "<table><tr><th>runner key</th><th>joined (Unix s)</th><th>checks an hour</th></tr>"
text cmrmore "The list shows the registered keys among the first 200 key files in the store, in the store's order."
text cmrunal "At least "
text cmrcap " The count stops after the first 200 keys in the store, so that showing this page stays cheap however many keys are made."
text cmr8 " The agreeing result has the same bytes as Interplane's own check."
text cmr9 " The agreeing result differs from Interplane's own check."
text cmr10 " Keys are free to make, so this is not called verified."
text cmdet "details"
text cmdot "."
text cmown "Interplane's own check: compiler omc <code>"
text cmownb "</code>, binary <code>"
text cmowno "</code>, output <code>"
text cmowne "</code>, exit 0."
text cmtab "<table><tr><th>key</th><th>time (Unix s)</th><th>exit</th><th>binary SHA-256</th><th>output SHA-256</th><th>signed message</th></tr>"
text cmtabe "</table>"
text cmtr "<tr><td class=\"mono\">"
text cmtd "</td><td class=\"mono\">"
text cmtre "</td></tr>"
text cmback "Back to community machines"
text cmback2 "The part in the salvage yard"
text cmtg2 "/g/"

note ---- counting
note cm_count: for part id, N (keys counted), K (largest agreeing group), the number of groups,
note whether two groups tie for largest, and whether the largest group's result equals the hub's
note own receipt (glrcpt: slpublic id must have been called)
fn cm_count id view uchar * to void
b = new uchar 8192 0
put cmgv cmcn 0
put cmgv cmck 0
put cmgv cmcg 0
put cmgv cmctie 0
put cmgv cmcagr 0
cm_p0
cm_pa cmtparts
cm_pa id
cm_pa cmtg2
fd = fopen cmpth 0 get cmgv cmpl 573440 0
if lt fd 0
ret
end
while true bound 9223372036854775807
n = getdnts int fd b 0 8192
if le n 0
break
end
o = ulong 0
while lt o ulong n bound 8192
o = add o cm_gent id part b o sub ulong n o
end
end
x = fclose int fd
end

note cm_gent: one entry of parts/<id>/g/: a "<hash>.v" file names a group
fn cm_gent id view uchar * d view uchar * to ulong
rl = or ulong get d 16 shl ulong get d 17 8
if lt rl 86
ret rl
end
if ne get d 85 0
ret rl
end
if not cm_eq part d 83 2 cmtv
ret rl
end
h = new uchar 64 0
for i ulong 64
put h i get d add 19 i
end
if not cm_ishex h
ret rl
end
c = cm_gsize id h
put cmgv cmcn add get cmgv cmcn c
put cmgv cmcg add get cmgv cmcg 1
k = get cmgv cmck
if gt c k
put cmgv cmck c
put cmgv cmctie 0
put cmgv cmcagr 0
if cm_vhub id h
put cmgv cmcagr 1
end
ret rl
end
if eq c k
put cmgv cmctie 1
end
ret rl
end

note cm_gsize: the number of keys in parts/<id>/g/<h>/
fn cm_gsize id view uchar * h view uchar * to ulong
b = new uchar 8192 0
cm_p0
cm_pa cmtparts
cm_pa id
cm_pa cmtg2
cm_pa h
fd = fopen cmpth 0 get cmgv cmpl 573440 0
if lt fd 0
ret 0
end
c = ulong 0
while true bound 9223372036854775807
n = getdnts int fd b 0 8192
if le n 0
break
end
c = add c cm_dcnt part b 0 ulong n
end
x = fclose int fd
ret c
end

note cm_dcnt: entries in a getdents64 buffer other than "." and ".."
fn cm_dcnt b view uchar * to ulong
o = ulong 0
c = ulong 0
while lt o len b bound 8192
rl = or ulong get b add o 16 shl ulong get b add o 17 8
if eq rl 0
ret c
end
dot = eq get b add o 19 46
d1 = and dot eq get b add o 20 0
d2 = and dot and eq get b add o 20 46 eq get b add o 21 0
if not or d1 d2
c = add c 1
end
o = add o rl
end
ret c
end

note cm_vhub: the group's triple equals the hub's receipt: binary, stdout, exit 0
fn cm_vhub id view uchar * h view uchar * to bool
b = new uchar 256 0
cm_p0
cm_pa cmtparts
cm_pa id
cm_pa cmtg2
cm_pa h
cm_pa cmtv
r = cm_rd b
if ne r 132
ret false
end
for i ulong 64
if ne get b i get glrcpt add 65 i
ret false
end
if ne get b add 65 i get glrcpt add 129 i
ret false
end
end
ret and eq get b 130 48 eq get b 131 10
end

note ---- the record line
fn cm_rline id view uchar * lk bool to void
cm_count id
n = get cmgv cmcn
fput cmp
if eq n 0
fput cmr0
fput cmpe
ret
end
k = get cmgv cmck
fput cmr1
fnum n
if eq n 1
fput cmr2
else
fput cmr2s
end
fput cmr3
fnum k
fput cmr4
if gt n k
fput cmr5
fnum sub n k
fput cmr6
else
fput cmdot
end
if eq get cmgv cmctie 1
fput cmr7
end
if and eq n k eq get cmgv cmcagr 1
fput cmr8
end
if and eq n k eq get cmgv cmcagr 0
fput cmr9
end
fput cmr10
if lk
fputc 32
cm_alink cmslpart id cmdet
end
fput cmpe
end

fn cm_alink a view uchar * id view uchar * t view uchar * to void
fput cmhref
fputb
fput a
fesc id
fput cmhrefe
fput t
fput cmae
end

note cm_partln: the line on the salvage part page (nothing when the community store is off)
fn cm_partln id view uchar * to void
if not cm_on
ret
end
fput cmh2
fput cmcmh
fput cmh2e
cm_rline id true
end

note ---- /community/
fn cm_index to long
id = new uchar 64 0
fput cmbase
fput cmh1
fput cmtitle
fput cmh1e
fput cmp
fput cmintro
fput cmpe
fput cmh2
fput cmjoinh
fput cmh2e
fput cmpre
fput cmjoin
fput cmpree
fput cmp
fput cmjoinp
fput cmpe
fput cmh2
fput cmplath
fput cmh2e
fput cmplat
fput cmh2
fput cmdoesh
fput cmh2e
fput cmdoes
fput cmh2
fput cmneverh
fput cmh2e
fput cmp
fput cmnever
fput cmpe
fput cmh2
fput cmstoph
fput cmh2e
fput cmpre
fput cmstop
fput cmpree
fput cmp
fput cmstopp
fput cmpe
fput cmh2
fput cmruleh
fput cmh2e
fput cmp
fput cmrule
fput cmpe
cm_runners
fput cmh2
fput cmpartsh
fput cmh2e
shown = ulong 0
n = get glidxn 0
for ix ulong n bound 1000000
pos = sub sub n ix 1
for i ulong 64
put id i get glidx add mul pos 65 i
end
if cm_ispart id
cm_pcard id
shown = add shown 1
end
end
if eq shown 0
fput cmp
fput cmnopart
fput cmpe
end
cm_devfoot
fput cmclose
ret 200
end

fn cm_ispart id view uchar * to bool
if not slpublic id
ret false
end
ret eq get glrec 8 2
end

note cm_pcard: the part's title (linking to the yard) and its record line
fn cm_pcard id view uchar * to void
fput cmcard
fput cmhref
fputb
fput cmslsal
fesc id
fput cmhrefe
slesc 1
fput cmae
cm_rline id true
fput cmcarde
end

fn cm_devfoot to void
fput cmh2
fput cmdevh
fput cmh2e
fput cmp
fput cmdev
fputc 32
fput cmhref
fputb
fput cmled
fputb
fput cmrefl
fputb
fput cmsums
fput cmh2
fput cmfilesh
fput cmh2e
fput cmpre
cm_sumsout
fput cmpree
fput cmp
fput cmolder
cm_archls
fput cmpe
end

note cm_archls: links to every ledger.<seconds> and refused.<seconds> in the store root
fn cm_archls to void
b = new uchar 8192 0
cm_p0
fd = fopen cmpth 0 get cmgv cmpl 573440 0
if lt fd 0
ret
end
while true bound 9223372036854775807
n = getdnts int fd b 0 8192
if le n 0
break
end
o = ulong 0
while lt o ulong n bound 8192
o = add o cm_archent part b o sub ulong n o
end
end
x = fclose int fd
end

fn cm_archent d view uchar * to ulong
nm = new uchar 64 0
n2 = new uchar 64 0
rl = or ulong get d 16 shl ulong get d 17 8
nl = ulong 0
while lt add 19 nl rl bound 256
if eq get d add 19 nl 0
break
end
nl = add nl 1
end
if or eq nl 0 gt nl 60
ret rl
end
for i ulong nl bound 64
put nm i get d add 19 i
end
if cm_archok part nm 0 nl
for i ulong nl bound 64
put n2 i get nm i
end
fputc 32
cm_alink cmslug part nm 0 nl part n2 0 nl
end
ret rl
end

note cm_sumsout: dist/SHA256SUMS, escaped
fn cm_sumsout to void
b = new uchar 4096 0
cm_q0
cm_pa cmtdist
cm_pa cmtsums
r = cm_rd b
if gt r 0
fesc part b 0 ulong r
end
end

note ---- /community/part/<id>
fn cm_partpage id view uchar * to long
if not cm_ispart id
ret 404
end
fput cmbase
fput cmp
cm_alink cmslug id cmback
fput cmpe
fput cmh1
slesc 1
fput cmh1e
cm_rline id false
fput cmp
cm_alink cmslsal id cmback2
fput cmpe
x = slpublic id
fput cmp
fput cmown
fput tlpin
fput cmownb
cm_rcp 65
fput cmowno
cm_rcp 129
fput cmowne
fput cmpe
fput cmtab
cm_rows id
fput cmtabe
fput cmclose
ret 200
end

fn cm_rcp o ulong to void
for i ulong 64
fputc get glrcpt add o i
end
end

note cm_rows: one table row per counted key (parts/<id>/k/<key>)
fn cm_rows id view uchar * to void
b = new uchar 8192 0
cm_p0
cm_pa cmtparts
cm_pa id
cm_pa cmtk
fd = fopen cmpth 0 get cmgv cmpl 573440 0
if lt fd 0
ret
end
while true bound 9223372036854775807
n = getdnts int fd b 0 8192
if le n 0
break
end
o = ulong 0
while lt o ulong n bound 8192
o = add o cm_row id part b o sub ulong n o
end
end
x = fclose int fd
end

note cm_row: a key's row from "<binary> <stdout> <exit> <time> <message sha>\n"
note The length test and the byte read are two ifs: or is eager in Omega, so a short entry ("." or
note "..", 24 bytes) that ends the getdents buffer would otherwise be read past its end at byte 83
note (trap 3; the live store lists ".." last, 2026-11-11).
fn cm_row id view uchar * d view uchar * to ulong
rl = or ulong get d 16 shl ulong get d 17 8
if lt rl 84
ret rl
end
if ne get d 83 0
ret rl
end
k = new uchar 64 0
b = new uchar 512 0
for i ulong 64
put k i get d add 19 i
end
if not cm_ishex k
ret rl
end
cm_p0
cm_pa cmtparts
cm_pa id
cm_pa cmtk
cm_pa k
r = cm_rd b
if lt r 140
ret rl
end
cm_rowout k part b 0 ulong r
ret rl
end

note cm_rowout: fields of b are binary(64) sp stdout(64) sp exit sp time sp msgsha(64) LF
fn cm_rowout k view uchar * b view uchar * to void
kk = new uchar 64 0
for i ulong 64
put kk i get k i
end
e = cm_spn b 130
t = cm_spn b add e 1
if gt add t 65 len b
ret
end
fput cmtr
cm_alink cmslkey k kk
fput cmtd
fesc part b add e 1 sub t add e 1
fput cmtd
fesc part b 130 sub e 130
fput cmtd
fesc part b 0 64
fput cmtd
fesc part b 65 64
fput cmtd
cm_alink cmslmsg part b add t 1 64 cmdet
fput cmtre
end

note cm_spn: the index of the first space in b at or after i (len b when none)
fn cm_spn b view uchar * i ulong to ulong
j = i
while lt j len b bound 512
if eq get b j 32
ret j
end
j = add j 1
end
ret j
end

note ---- runners now (on /community/): the registered keys and Interplane's note on its own runners
note cmkc: keys counted (first pass) or rows written (second pass)
note cmke: key entries looked at in this pass; cmkcap: 1 when a pass stopped at cmkmax entries. Keys
note are free to make, so each pass reads at most cmkmax key files (one forged serves every request).
const cmkc ulong 15
const cmke ulong 16
const cmkcap ulong 17
const cmkmax ulong 200
fn cm_runners to void
put cmgv cmkc 0
put cmgv cmke 0
put cmgv cmkcap 0
cm_kscan 0
n = get cmgv cmkc
capped = get cmgv cmkcap
fput cmh2
fput cmrunh
fput cmh2e
fput cmp
if eq capped 1
fput cmrunal
end
fnum n
if eq n 1
fput cmrun1
else
fput cmrun1s
end
fput cmrun2
if eq capped 1
fput cmrcap
end
fput cmpe
note the note is a file the operator writes in the read-only root (beside deny); absent: no note
b = new uchar 2048 0
cm_q0
cm_pa cmtnote
r = cm_rd b
if gt r 0
fput cmp
fput cmnoteh
fesc part b 0 ulong r
fput cmpe
end
if eq n 0
ret
end
fput cmrtab
put cmgv cmkc 0
put cmgv cmke 0
put cmgv cmkcap 0
cm_kscan 1
fput cmtabe
if eq capped 1
fput cmp
fput cmrmore
fput cmpe
end
end

note cm_kscan: every entry of keys/; m 0 counts registered keys, m 1 writes their rows (first 200)
fn cm_kscan m ulong to void
b = new uchar 8192 0
cm_p0
cm_pa cmtkeys
fd = fopen cmpth 0 get cmgv cmpl 573440 0
if lt fd 0
ret
end
while true bound 9223372036854775807
n = getdnts int fd b 0 8192
if le n 0
break
end
o = ulong 0
while lt o ulong n bound 8192
o = add o cm_kent part b o sub ulong n o m
end
note stop once the entry cap is hit (cmkcap). Not on the row count: the counting pass must see the
note 201st key entry to know it stopped early, else 200 keys would be shown as an exact count.
if eq get cmgv cmkcap 1
break
end
end
x = fclose int fd
end

note cm_kent: one entry of keys/. A registered key file is "<public key, 130 hex> <rate> <time> j\n"
note (cm_kwrite). Every length test is its own if before the read it protects (or and and are eager).
fn cm_kent d view uchar * m ulong to ulong
rl = or ulong get d 16 shl ulong get d 17 8
if lt rl 84
ret rl
end
if ne get d 83 0
ret rl
end
k = new uchar 64 0
for i ulong 64
put k i get d add 19 i
end
if not cm_ishex k
ret rl
end
e = get cmgv cmke
if ge e cmkmax
put cmgv cmkcap 1
ret rl
end
put cmgv cmke add e 1
cm_krow k m
ret rl
end

note cm_krow: key k counted (m 0) or its row written (m 1) when keys/<k> is a registered key file
fn cm_krow k view uchar * m ulong to void
b = new uchar 512 0
cm_p0
cm_pa cmtkeys
cm_pa k
r = cm_rd b
if lt r 137
ret
end
n = ulong r
if ne get b sub n 1 10
ret
end
if ne get b sub n 2 106
ret
end
if ne get b sub n 3 32
ret
end
c = get cmgv cmkc
if eq m 0
put cmgv cmkc add c 1
ret
end
if ge c 200
ret
end
e = cm_spn part b 0 n 131
if ge e sub n 3
ret
end
t = cm_spn part b 0 n add e 1
if ne t sub n 3
ret
end
put cmgv cmkc add c 1
kk = new uchar 64 0
for i ulong 64
put kk i get k i
end
fput cmtr
cm_alink cmslkey k kk
fput cmtd
fesc part b add e 1 sub t add e 1
fput cmtd
fesc part b 131 sub e 131
fput cmtre
end
